{"title":"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A two-digit integer between 10 and 99, inclusive, is chosen at random. Each possible integer is equally likely to be chosen. What is the probability that its tens digit is a multiple of its units (ones) digit?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fcbd2792814bde68272aa7c1f87c41717448f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99 - 10 + 1 = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> possible two-digit numbers in total.\n</p><p>Next, we can find the number of values such that the tens digit is a multiple of the units digit by using cases for each units digit.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values if the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the only possible multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, if the tens digit was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the number wouldn't be a two-digit number.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values if the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because all possible digits for the tens digit (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values if the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the tens digit must be even, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such values: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values if the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the tens digit must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such values: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values if the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the tens digit must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such values: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible value if the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a6e5f37861d1d64b0a6afdd09ab2fad7644680a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 2 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, which goes over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the tens digit must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, if the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the tens digit must be equal to the ones digit, so each of these cases gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values in total.\n</p><p>This means that in total, the number of two-digit values where the tens digit is a multiple of the units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec060d56ea148a691cc665f8659466c94924f6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 9 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 5 = 9 + 7 + 7 = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"306\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The probability of choosing such a number if a random two-digit number is chosen is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2962b5041104f2c039607787efb25b71ef3f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{23}{90}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC\">2016 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_6\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 6\">Team Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Team Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Individual 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3\">Individual 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4\">Individual 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5\">Individual 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Individual 6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Individual 7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Individual 8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Individual 9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Individual 10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_A\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 0 Problem A\">Relay 0 A</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 0 Problem B (page does not exist)\">Relay 0 B</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 0 Problem C (page does not exist)\">Relay 0 C</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_A&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem A (page does not exist)\">Relay 1 A</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem B (page does not exist)\">Relay 1 B</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem C (page does not exist)\">Relay 1 C</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_2_Problem_A&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 2 Problem A (page does not exist)\">Relay 2 A</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_2_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 2 Problem B (page does not exist)\">Relay 2 B</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_2_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 2 Problem C (page does not exist)\">Relay 2 C</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.